 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Rules are deferred while the bundle is defined, then replayed onto the app when it's registered. All paths below are under `src/tessel/sansio/`.\n\n1. **`Bundle.attach_route_rule`** (`bundles.py:413`) validates that the endpoint and view name contain no dots. It doesn't touch the app. It calls `self.record(lambda s: s.attach_route_rule(...))`.\n2. **`Bundle.record`** (`bundles.py:224`) appends that callback to `Bundle.deferred_functions`.\n3. **`App.register_bundle`** (`app.py:571`) is what you call on the app. It calls `bundle.register(app, options)`.\n4. **`Bundle.register`** (`bundles.py:273`) builds a `BundleSetupState` via `make_setup_state` (`bundles.py:246`), then runs `for deferred in self.deferred_functions: deferred(state)` (`bundles.py:334`).\n5. **`BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule`** (`bundles.py:87`) applies the bundle's changes and calls `self.app.attach_route_rule(...)`:\n   - it prepends `url_prefix` to the rule;\n   - it defaults `subdomain`;\n   - it merges `url_defaults`;\n   - it prefixes the endpoint with `<name_prefix>.<bundle name>.`.\n6. **`App.attach_route_rule`** (`app.py:606`) registers the final rule on the app's URL map.",
